course: dictionary
lesson: 14296
title: Words about food and feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nourishing is a word about food, and it can also describe things that are good for your mind. When food is nourishing, it has the things your body needs to grow and stay healthy. «The nourishing soup warmed Sam up when he had a cold.» Soup that is nourishing is full of good things, not just warm and tasty.
explain: Nourish is the verb, the action word. «Sunlight and water nourish the young plants.» The plants get what they need to grow, so nourish means to give food or care that helps something grow. Nourishes, nourished and nourishing are all forms of the same word.
explain: You can also use nourishing when you talk about things that feed your mind or feelings. «The story was nourishing, and it made me think about kindness.» A nourishing book is good for your thinking, the way a nourishing meal is good for your body.
fact: Nourishing means full of the things your body needs to grow and stay healthy.
fact: «Nourish» is a verb: it means to give food or care that helps something grow.
fact: A balanced, nourishing meal often has vegetables, protein and whole grains.
fact: «Nourishing» can also describe a book, a story or an idea that is good for your mind or feelings.
fact: Nourishing and tasty are not the same: a sweet treat can taste good but may not be nourishing.
exercise: «The nourishing soup warmed Sam up when he had a cold.» What does nourishing mean? | Cheap to buy in the shops | Left over from yesterday | Very salty and hot | *Full of the things your body needs to grow and stay healthy
exercise: «Sunlight and water nourish the young plants.» What does nourish mean here? | Paint in bright colours | Hide from the light | Cut down and remove | *Give what helps something grow
exercise: Which food is the most nourishing? | *Lentil and vegetable stew | Fizzy drink | Packet of crisps | Bag of sweets
test: «The story was nourishing, and it made me think about kindness.» What does nourishing mean when it describes a story? | Wet and soggy | *Good for your mind or feelings | Very loud and noisy | Full of food
test: Nadia says nourishing is just another word for tasty. Why is that not quite right? | *Nourishing means good for you, not just nice to taste | Nourishing means sweet | Nourishing means cooked in a pan | Nourishing means tasting nice, so it is the same word
exam: Which word in «Mum made a nourishing meal full of beans and vegetables for us all» tells you the meal is good for your body? | vegetables | meal | *nourishing | beans
